---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Telemedicine & Teleconsultation"
  subtitle="Terms of use and informed consent for online consultations, in line with the Telemedicine Practice Guidelines, 2020."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. About Teleconsultation</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name} offers teleconsultation as an alternative to an in-person visit for suitable, non-emergency conditions.
    Teleconsultation is provided by a registered medical practitioner in accordance with the
    <strong>Telemedicine Practice Guidelines, 2020</strong> notified under the Indian Medical Council (Professional Conduct,
    Etiquette and Ethics) Regulations, 2002, and any subsequent amendments.
  </p>

  <h2>2. When Teleconsultation Is Suitable</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Follow-up reviews of an existing condition where an in-person examination is not essential.</li>
    <li>Review of test or investigation reports and advice on the next steps.</li>
    <li>Minor, stable or self-limiting complaints where a physical examination is not indicated.</li>
    <li>Second opinions and lifestyle or preventive-health guidance.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. When Teleconsultation Is NOT Suitable</h2>
  <p>
    Teleconsultation is <strong>not</strong> a substitute for emergency care. Do not use it for any medical emergency.
    If you experience chest pain, severe breathlessness, stroke symptoms, uncontrolled bleeding, serious injury, severe
    allergic reaction, or any rapidly worsening condition, call our emergency line
    <strong>{hospital.phones.emergency}</strong> or dial <strong>112</strong> immediately (ambulance <strong>108</strong>).
  </p>

  <h2>4. Informed Consent</h2>
  <p>
    By requesting a teleconsultation you confirm that you understand and consent to the following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The consultation is conducted remotely using audio and/or video, and the doctor cannot perform a physical examination.</li>
    <li>Diagnosis and treatment may therefore be more limited, and the doctor may advise an in-person visit or further tests if required.</li>
    <li>You will provide accurate and complete information about your symptoms, medical history, current medicines and allergies.</li>
    <li>You may withdraw consent and end the consultation at any time.</li>
    <li>Clinical records of the consultation will be created and retained as required by law.</li>
    <li>Technology may occasionally fail or the connection may drop; the doctor will attempt to reconnect or reschedule.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Prescriptions</h2>
  <p>
    Prescribing rules follow the Telemedicine Practice Guidelines. Depending on the category of medicine, the doctor may
    issue a prescription, advise an in-person consultation, or decline to prescribe. Medicines in the prohibited category
    for teleconsultation will not be prescribed remotely. Where permitted, a digital prescription may be shared with you,
    and you may be asked to visit the hospital for certain treatments.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Identity and Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    The doctor will verify your identity before the consultation using the details you provide. Your consultation is
    confidential and follows the same privacy standards as an in-person visit. Please see our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Fees and Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Teleconsultation fees are as communicated at the time of booking. Unless otherwise stated, teleconsultation fees are
    not refundable once the consultation has taken place. See our
    <a href="/refund-cancellation">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Technical Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A stable internet connection and a smartphone, tablet or computer with a working camera and microphone.</li>
    <li>A private, quiet place where you can speak freely.</li>
    <li>Your previous prescriptions, reports and a list of current medicines where relevant.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Doctor's Right to Decline</h2>
  <p>
    A doctor may decline or discontinue a teleconsultation if it is not clinically appropriate, if identity cannot be
    verified, or if the consultation falls outside the permitted scope. In such cases, the fee may be refunded in
    accordance with our refund policy, and you will be advised on the appropriate next step.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    Teleconsultation advice is based on the information you provide and what is observable remotely. To the extent
    permitted by law, the hospital and treating doctor are not liable for outcomes arising from incomplete or inaccurate
    information provided by the patient, or from the patient's failure to follow referred advice for in-person evaluation
    or emergency care.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Record Keeping</h2>
  <p>
    Teleconsultation records are maintained in accordance with the Telemedicine Practice Guidelines and applicable law, and
    are kept confidential. You may request a copy of your consultation record through the hospital.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name}<br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}, {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    Email: {hospital.email} · Phone: {hospital.phones.appointment}
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
